#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""KOAN, the rule-discovery puzzle, as one file. Version 1.0.0, gen 1.

Find the master's hidden rule about koans (rows of 1 to 6 digits, each 1 2 3 or 4), one
shell command at a time. Start here:

    python3 koan.py            what this is
    python3 koan.py help       how to play (one page)
    python3 koan.py new        a new puzzle

Use python instead of python3 if that is the name on your machine. Each move is one command;
the game saves after every command, next to this file in .save, or in <temp>/koan when this
folder cannot be written. GAME_HOME=/some/folder chooses the save folder.

This file holds the game's modules as plain text (the dictionary below) and a small importer
that runs them. Nothing is downloaded and nothing outside the save folder is written.
Built by tools/build_onefile.py from engine/ (sources sha256 d3f5af11db84ad6b).
KOAN. Directed by Catbunlore. Made with Claude. MIT licence.
"""
